{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252398,"nonce":"MEAqWjAcsl3dnrIRaw628WJSJQE=","title":"Check on a run that Garmin records the footpod's serial and software version","message":"Garmin Connect lists the watch and HRM 600 after a run but not the footpod. fit-inspect on a\nrun (2026-11-19) showed the watch records the footpod in the FIT file, but with no manufacturer,\nproduct or software version, and the hex serial cut to `44`: it parses these as numbers. The\nfirmware now sends a decimal serial number, a `major.minor` firmware revision and a PnP ID\n(pid.codes test ID).\n\nRun fit-inspect on the next run's FIT file: are the serial and software version recorded, and does a\nmanufacturer appear? Does Garmin Connect list the footpod now?","files":null}]}